WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
I know it's infuriating when
anyone presents both sides of an issue

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.600
and says: "let the audience decide".

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.480
And I don't really like doing meta stuff
where I talk about

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.040
the process of making videos,
but I can't find any other way

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.360
to give enough context
to make this video work.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.160
Hence the "come for a walk with me

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.600
through a rough bit of the English
countryside" GoPro camera shot.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.080
It's important to break the format
visually as well.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.520
I've been sharing videos from around
Germany, Austria and Switzerland

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.840
over the past couple of weeks.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.900
One of the first things I filmed on
that trip was the

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.520
radon tunnel, the "radonstollen", in Bad
Kreuznach in south-west Germany.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.280
The video should have gone out weeks ago.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.560
But despite filming
going really well on location, despite

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.600
being really happy with my script
and the interview at the time,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.520
I just wasn't comfortable with it
when I got back here to the UK.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.800
Radon, or "rad-don" if you're German,
is a colorless, odorless, radioactive gas

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.640
that's produced naturally by uranium decay.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.240
All around the world, tiny tiny
amounts of it seep out from

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.080
wide areas of the ground and get diluted
into the atmosphere harmlessly.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.880
But if your house is in a particularly bad
radon area, like here in Oxfordshire,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.360
then you can get detectors installed
or tests done to check that

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.000
radon isn't building up inside your house
and exposing you to too much radiation.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.600
Which is why I was surprised
that there are a few places in the world

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.480
where people go to be exposed to radon
deliberately for pain relief.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.960
So: the radon tunnel in Bad Kreuznach.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.840
- It is a tunnel that was founded 1775.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.120
People tried to find mercury here.
They dug for mercury.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:42.240
They did never find mercury, but round about
110 years ago, they found radon.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:48.620
The dose is, per one hour treatment,
between 30-60 thousand bequerels.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.600
On average you need
ten treatments, one hour.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:59.720
At the end, the application will have
a dose of around about 2.2 millisieverts.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.840
To give you an idea
what is the equivalent:

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.840
if you have, for instance,
X-rays of your hip or your knee,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.680
it is more or less the same, equivalent.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:15.800
A complete CT of the complete body
has about between 20 and 40 millisieverts.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.440
- Every medically trained person
that I've talked to about radon therapy,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.400
they've all gone through the same
three stages that I did.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.020
First of all, complete skepticism,
"oh, that sounds like a bad idea".

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.360
Certainly, most of the world
would consider deliberate exposure

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.240
to radioactive gas for pain relief
as alternative medicine.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.520
That's what I did.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.840
And then stage two.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.080
You look at the scientific papers
and, yes, the marketing,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.080
that talk about what limited trials
there have been, and the patient

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.320
testimonials, and the theories about why
it works, and the reaction becomes...

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.860
agh, I guess maybe it's worth a look?

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.120
But there's a conflict
of interest declaration in that paper.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.120
But it says the funders had no say
in the results or the release.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.440
And there is almost a folk belief
in some parts of the nuclear industry,

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.080
particularly in the US, about something
called "radiation hormesis", where

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.640
very small doses of radiation
can have a beneficial effect, they think,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.860
because they cause repair systems
in your body to kick into action.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.000
But that is an idea, a hypothesis.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.800
It's not even really a theory yet.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.760
It's not been properly tested.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.000
All the major international authorities
say that it's entirely unproven

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.780
and there isn't really any truly safe
dose of radiation.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.440
And yet, radon therapy seems
to work for a lot of people.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.480
So then you've reached the third stage:

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.120
not knowing how to even talk about this
responsibly.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.240
That's where I'm at.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.360
I've met the people who run a radon tunnel.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.000
I've talked to a patient.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.280
I've got a duty of care to them,
as I do to anyone I film with.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.240
But I also have a duty to the audience

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.080
and to the truth: scientific
or historical or personal.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.120
So I need to make something very clear.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.320
This is not an endorsement.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.080
I think radon therapy is fascinating.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.600
The people who run the radon spa
definitely think it works.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.640
Certainly, most of their patients do.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.760
There's just enough evidence here
that this unqualified skeptic

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.320
can't write it off, not immediately.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.320
And the fact that there's all this
infrastructure for handling radioactive gas

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:17.320
as part of something that
most of the world hasn't even heard of?

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.120
Well, I think that's interesting enough
to at least discuss.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.440
- Just to make clear:
it is not "wellness", it's not miracles.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.680
We do not promise something weird.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.720
It is pure medicine.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.560
It's a medical application
where you need a doctor's prescription.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:39.080
And at the end, 85% of the patients,
they report it helped, it worked.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:44.640
So you get rid of your medication
for pain relievers for one year and more.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:50.160
It is not wellness. That's really...  it must be clear.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:54.280
Obviously, to get a license for this,
especially in Germany,

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.360
it's a really huge
and complicated process,

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:03.040
and therefore we have to prove
that the minimum application of the doses

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.720
is not below 30,000Bq and the maximum dose
is never above 100,000Bq.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.720
We are always, in the average,
somewhere between

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.200
30-60 thousand, which is a perfect range
for the treatment.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.320
- There are plenty of doctors
and health insurance companies in Germany

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.200
that endorse radon therapy,
but that isn't evidence for it working.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.680
The British National Health Service paid

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:31.680
for some homeopathic treatments
until 2017, despite a mountain of evidence

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.040
proving that homeopathy does
absolutely nothing.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.960
Homeopathy may feel like it works
for some people, but if you just

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.240
give people a sugar pill, a placebo,
and say "it'll help with your pain",

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.840
a lot of the time feels like it does help,
at least for the short term.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.760
The placebo effect isn't quite as magical
as some folks think,

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.440
but certainly very powerful for sensations
like pain and nausea...

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.400
the sort of things
that radon therapy is intended to treat.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:02.040
But the trouble is that radon spas aren't
like homeopathy or like magnet therapy.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.640
They're not popular enough
to have been comprehensively tested.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:10.500
Anecdotes are not evidence for something
medical, particularly when radiation is involved.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.840
The warning signs  of quackery, of fake medicine, are:
bold claims about miracle cures;

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.120
single interventions that claim to help
wildly different conditions;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.120
or explanations
that defy the laws of physics.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.560
It's not guaranteed to be quackery

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.760
if you've got those, of course,
but those are the warning signs.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.440
In other parts of the world, radon
therapy is much less regulated.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:37.200
In Montana, USA, say, there are old radon-filled
mines that just charge admission to go sit inside.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:45.280
And some of them make wild claims about helping
diabetes, gout, asthma, MS or even cancer.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.520
But the claims made in Germany
are much more limited and specific.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.400
It's just for relief of chronic pain,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:55.160
and the cause of chronic pain
can often be a mystery.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.840
And so can how to treat it.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.600
- The treatment doesn't work instantly,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.680
so if you leave the tunnel,
you are not instantly cured.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:09.800
Patients, they report to us, normally
it takes some days, up to 6-8 weeks,

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.040
when it works.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:16.600
We are aware that some other tunnels
worldwide, they claim they can cure anything.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:21.640
We are pain relief,
pain relief from inflammatory process.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.080
Not more and not less.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.440
Normally, people think "radioactivity,

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:31.480
oh, that's harmful!" but it is always
the same question: it's the doses

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.480
that makes sense, and what we here apply.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:41.760
You see this equipment that is monitoring
how much radon is emitted,

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.600
and we do emit radon in that quantity

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:51.280
that is necessary to initiate healing
processes.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.560
- There's one line
in that big analysis paper

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.800
that says it's really difficult to do
a fully double-blind study about this.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.640
That would be
where each patient doesn't know

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.440
if they're receiving radon or not,
and neither do the staff or the doctors.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:06.440
Yes, radon is colorless and odorless, but
it's always there, coming out the ground.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:11.040
You can't fool people into walking
into a somehow-identical tunnel or cabin

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.920
that you've just mysteriously constructed
next door to the old one,

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.360
but that doesn't happen
to have radon in it this time.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:21.520
Except: in that one tunnel in Bad
Kreuznach, you can turn off the radon.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.440
- This is absolutely unique,
and to my knowledge,

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.400
no other tunnel worldwide
has the same technique.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.000
And that is why we are, today,
absolutely safe.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.800
As you see on the monitor,
we have no radioactivity here

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.440
besides the normal activity
you have outside.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:42.080
The radon gas is emitted very deep down

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.960
in that mountain
and it is naturally emitted.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:52.600
At the end,
we just grab the gas with with a pipeline

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:57.040
and a kind of fan
that transports it into this room.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:01.680
And we can switch it on and off
in the proportion we need it.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.720
- That's why I was allowed to film
in the treatment room.

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.400
It didn't have any radon in it.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.080
Not then, anyway.
It hadn't been used for hours.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.200
All the ventilation meant
there was just fresh air in there.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.840
It would absolutely be possible

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:15.080
to set up a proper, large-scale,
double-blind study in that tunnel.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.440
If some university or government
wanted to fund it.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.080
If they could find enough
willing patients.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:20.720
If their ethics review board

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.520
would be willing to sign off
on treating people with radioactive gas.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:29.720
And if it could be arranged that no-one,
not even the staff at the tunnel,

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:33.600
knew whether each patient was getting
radon therapy or just fresh air.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.120
It would be difficult.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:39.480
But it's more possible there than anywhere
else, and I want that trial to happen.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:43.480
That's why I decided to talk about this
and put the video out.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:47.640
That's why I'm willing to risk
giving an audience to something

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.240
that isn't proven yet,
because if that works as claimed,

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.760
even just for some people with chronic pain,
it'd be brilliant.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.760
Very minor radiation
exposure is a risk that

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.640
a lot of people would be willing to take,
clearly are willing to take,

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:05.440
if they can't get pain relief
any other way.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:11.200
And if it doesn't work, then we  probably
need to stop exposing people to radiation?

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.520
I know it's a cop-out to say
"more studies are required".

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:19.240
It's the weak ending to every inconclusive
undergraduate paper,

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:21.400
but in this case, it's true.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:26.200
More studies are required, and hopefully
those studies will happen soon.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.920
Because I would love to go back
to a radon spa in a few years' time

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.860
and follow up with the proof.

